;;; A conclusion whose relation is a parameter its activator binds to `eq` is
;;; stored as a fact — regression `relvar-eq-assert`
;;; (`corpus/regressions.toml`), under Q-M1e2.26.
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; One fact `(p a)` and a rule concluding `(?R ?x w)` from `(p ?x)`,
;;; activated by `(r eq)`: `assert-eq-x-w`'s conclusion, its relation
;;; written as a parameter.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Under `(r eq)` the conclusion is `(eq ?x w)`, checked as `assert-eq-x-w`'s
;;; is (Q-M1e2.26): at root `r` concludes `(eq a w)`, which is false, so root is a
;;; contradiction: its core is `(p a)` and `refuted by` names `r`. R is empty.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `dc4c0bdc`, release and debug alike: the conclusion was stored, root
;;; held `(eq a w :rule r)` (`ein saturate FILE --dump`), and R was two
;;; states, ∅ and `{(p w)}`, exit 0 (`ein solve FILE`, `ein oracle FILE`).

(relation p Node :why "{?1} is a node")
(p a)
(rule r (?R)
  :match (p ?x)
  :assert (?R ?x w)
  :why "{?x} and w are in the relation {?R}")
(r eq)
